      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Several win chances. POWER MAIDEN (7) scored her maiden win five back and is poised to salute again after finishing in the money at the last three outings, most recently when second over 850m at Gladstone. Has the pace to settle in the leading division. Among the leading chances. AMPHAWA (1) finished 7 lengths back in eighth over 1000m at Nanango in open class last time out after a gutsy win two runs back. Super honest at course and distance and back in grade for this. BRAIDWOOD PRINCE (3) has not appeared since he finished fourth over 850m at Bundaberg on June 20. Four time winner course and distance and can go close fresh. NINE CIGARS (4) turned in a fine effort to win by 0.7 lengths at this course and distance when resuming from a spell last start. Finds another suitable race and can figure in the finish. LATE NIGHT TALKING (6) is also a last-start winner who can measure up again.",
